      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "selepas seksyen 88, seksyen baru 88A yang berikut: Penalty 88A. Any person who makes any statement for giving which is false in any material particular in any false return, claim, application, declaration or other statement. document which is requested or authorised to be made by or under the provisions of this Act or of any by-laws made thereunder shall be guilty of an offence and shall, on conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding five thousand ringgit.\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "27",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27__subsec_2",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27__subsec_3"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "Akta ibu adalah dipinda dengan memasukkan,"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "selepas seksyen 89, seksyen baru 89A dan 89B yang berikut: Commis- 89A. (1) When any person without lawful sion to excuse refuses or neglects to obey any recover expenses direction lawfully given under this Act or any incurred by laws made thereunder, the Commission for act done may, irrespective of whether any proceedings pursuant have been instituted against or any punishment to a lawful direction. RANG UNDANG-UNDANG imposed on such person for the refusal or neglect, do or cause to be done all such acts as are in its opinion reasonable or necessary for the purpose of carrying out such direction."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "The powers conferred by subsection (1) include the power to hire and employ such persons as are necessary and proper for making good whatever loss or damage that has been caused by any refusal or neglect of the person to whom the direction has been given."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27__subsec_3",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "3",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_27",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "Any expenses incurred in the exercise of the powers conferred under subsection (1) or (2) shall be recoverable from the person to whom the direction had been given as a civil debt. 89B. Where an offence under this Act or under any of the regulations or by laws made thereunder is committed by a body corporate (whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted), every director, secretary or manager of the body corporate shall be deemed to be guilty of the offence unless he proves that the offence was committed without his consent or connivance and that he exercised all due diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he ought to have exercised having regard to the nature of his functions in that capacity and to all the circumstances of the case.\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@/~cl_28",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "28",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/2/msa@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "Akta ibu adalah dipinda dengan memasukkan,"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "ms",
        "@value": "selepas seksyen 90, seksyen baru 90A dan 90B yang 90A. (1) The General Manager or such person as may be authorised by him may board any vessel within the port whenever he suspects that an offence under this Act or any by laws made thereunder has been or is about to be committed on board such vessel or SURUHANJAYA PELABUHAN PULAU PINANG 9 (PINDAAN) whenever he considers it necessary to do so in the discharge of his duties under this Act or any by-laws made thereunder. (2) The General Manager or such person as may be authorised by him may, in exercising his powers and carrying out his duties under subsection (1), seize any article, document or thing which he has reasonable grounds for believing has been used for the commission of, or is the subject matter of, or is required for the purpose of investigation and prosecution of, an offence under this Act or any by-laws made thereunder. (3) Any master of such vessel who wilfully delays, fails to comply with any order lawfully given, withholds any information or obstructs in any manner whatsoever the General Manager or such person as may be authorised by him pursuant to subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall, on conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding one thousand ringgit. 90B. (1) In the event of fire breaking out on board any vessel in the port, the General Manager or any person authorised by him may proceed to board the vessel with such persons and assistance as may seem fit to him and may give such orders to the master of the vessel as are necessary for scuttling the vessel or for removing that vessel or any other vessel, and he may take such other measures as are necessary and proper for the protection of life or property. (2) If the orders given pursuant to subsection (1) are not carried out forthwith by the master of the vessel, the General Manager or the person authorised by him may himself proceed to carry the orders into effect. RANG UNDANG-UNDANG (3) Any expenses incurred in the exercise of the powers conferred by subsections (1) and (2) shall be recoverable from the master or the owner of the vessel concerned as a civil debt.\"."
      }
    },
